# SQLite for local dev (zero config). To switch to Postgres for production,
# change the datasource provider in prisma/schema.prisma to "postgresql" and
# point this at a Postgres connection string instead.
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"

# Required for the AI concierge (chat + WhatsApp agent) to respond.
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com/
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""

# --- WhatsApp self-service onboarding (Meta Embedded Signup) ---
# See README's "WhatsApp self-service onboarding" section before touching
# these — they only work once HeyTable itself is registered as a Meta Tech
# Provider, which is a one-time business-verification step on Meta's side,
# not something set up per restaurant.
#
# WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN: any string you choose; used once to verify the
# webhook URL when you register it in the Meta App dashboard.
#
# META_APP_ID / META_APP_SECRET: from your Meta App's Basic Settings.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_META_APP_ID / NEXT_PUBLIC_META_CONFIG_ID: same App ID (client-
# visible by design — Meta's own JS SDK requires it) plus the Embedded
# Signup configuration ID you create under that app's WhatsApp product.
#
# Until META_APP_ID/META_APP_SECRET are set, the dashboard's "Connect
# WhatsApp" section shows a clear "not configured" state instead of a
# broken button, and outbound replies are logged to the console instead of
# actually sent (see lib/channels/whatsapp.ts).
WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN=""
META_APP_ID=""
META_APP_SECRET=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_APP_ID=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_CONFIG_ID=""
